@node Features
@chapter Features

@cindex Features

Casual Avy is designed to bring discoverability to many Avy commands for an enhanced navigation and editing experience.

@image{images/casual-avy-screenshot,,,,png}

@itemize
@item
Avy editing commands allow for working with a remote region or line while keeping the current point in place.

@item
Avy navigation commands allow for granular navigation to different syntactic entities (things).
@end itemize

@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

@cindex Requirements

Casual Avy requires usage of
@itemize
@item
Avy ≥ 0.5.0
@item
Casual ≥ 3.0.0
@end itemize

Casual Avy has been verified with the following configuration. 
@itemize
@item
GNU Emacs 31.1 (macOS 15.7@comma{} Ubuntu Linux 22.04.5 LTS)
@item
Avy 0.5.0
@end itemize

@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install
@vindex casual-avy-tmenu
@vindex casual-avy-keybinding
@vindex package-install
@vindex casual-init-hook
@vindex casual-init

Casual Avy is intended to be installed via @code{package-install} from MELPA@comma{} either directly or as a dependency to Casual Suite. After this installation@comma{} Casual Avy can be setup in a number of ways@comma{} as enumerated in the sub-sections below.

The design intent for using Casual Avy is to setup a global keybinding to the Transient menu @code{casual-avy-tmenu}. This keybinding is specified by the customizable variable @code{casual-avy-keybinding} which is by default set to @code{M-g} and can be changed to user preference.

@menu
* Setup with Casual Suite::
* Setup with Casual only::
* Setup Casual Avy only::
* Manual Install::
@end menu

@node Setup with Casual Suite
@section Setup with Casual Suite

If you have Casual Avy installed as a dependency to Casual Suite @ref{Top,,,casual-suite,}@comma{} then Casual Suite will automatically setup Casual Avy. Refer to the Casual Suite Install Section @ref{Install,,,casual-suite,} for more detail. 

Note that this will only work if Casual Avy is installed via @code{package-install}.

@node Setup with Casual only
@section Setup with Casual only

Casual Avy includes the base Casual package as a dependency. Casual has the command @code{casual-init} which will setup all modules within it as specified in the hook variable @code{casual-init-hook}. Casual Avy can be included in this hook with the following Elisp added to your Emacs initialization file:

@lisp
(add-hook 'casual-init-hook #'casual-avy-init)
@end lisp

Note that this will only work if Casual Avy is installed via @code{package-install}.

@node Setup Casual Avy only
@section Setup Casual Avy only

If only setup for Casual Avy is desired@comma{} then directly run the command @code{casual-avy-init}@comma{} either manually with @code{extended-execute-command} (@code{M-x}) or by adding it to your Emacs initialization file.

@lisp
(casual-avy-init)
@end lisp

Note that this will only work if Casual Avy is installed via @code{package-install}.

@node Manual Install
@section Manual Install

Casual Avy is installed outside of @code{package-install}@comma{} then the 

@lisp
(require 'casual-avy) ;; optional if using autoloaded menu
(keymap-global-set casual-avy-keybinding #'casual-avy-tmenu)
@end lisp

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@cindex Usage

@image{images/casual-avy-screenshot,,,,png}

Invoke the Casual Avy menu (@code{casual-avy-tmenu}) with the keybinding @code{casual-avy-keybinding} (default @code{M-g}).

The menu is grouped into the following sections:

@itemize
@item
Scope — Set scope for Avy command to apply to either above or below the current point.
@item
Goto Thing — Navigate to text @emph{thing}.
@item
Goto Line — Navigate to a line.
@item
Edit Other Line — Line-based Avy editing commands.
@item
Edit Other Region — Region-based Avy editing commands.
@item
Index — Imenu and index-related commands.
@item
Occur/Grep/Error — Navigation commands for Occur@comma{} Grep@comma{} or Error.
@end itemize

Avy editing commands allow for editing a different line or region while @emph{keeping the point stationary}. The following glossary details the meaning of the menu labels under the @strong{Edit} sections.

@table @asis
@item Copy
Copies the selected object (line@comma{} region) into the kill ring.
@item Kill
Kills the selected object into the kill ring.
@item Move to above current line
Moves the selected object to the line above the current point.
@item Duplicate to above current line
Duplicates the selected object to the line above the current point.
@end table

